+	// Matrix-scan robustness (kbdfix, 2026-08-18). The base matrix scanner
+	// samples one row per tick and reports make/break in row-then-column
+	// order, so a modifier (Shift/Ctrl/Alt) and the character it qualifies,
+	// pressed inside the same scan cycle, can reach the guest with the
+	// character AHEAD of its modifier — the guest then latches the unshifted
+	// key (HUP->HUp, shift-7 & ->7, $HOME->$hOME). We buffer one cycle's key
+	// edges and flush them modifiers-first on press / modifiers-last on
+	// release, so the level is always established before (and torn down after)
+	// the character regardless of where each sits in the matrix. Purely an
+	// ordering of events already produced this cycle; adds at most one scan
+	// period (~0.83 ms) of latency and never reorders same-class edges.
+	static bool code_is_modifier(u8 code);
+	void flush_pending_keys();
 
